From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wminet_utils: what .NET's System.Management calls for WMI (5943)

wminet_utils: what .NET's System.Management calls for WMI

System.Management (the .NET package; .NET Framework's own too) loads
<InstallRoot>\v4.0.30319\wminet_utils.dll and looks up 50 functions by name.
Without it every use of System.Management threw at its first type
initializer: DYMO Connect's launcher crashed at start ("Failed to load
required native library ...\Framework64\v4.0.30319\wminet_utils.dll"), as
would any .NET program that asks WMI anything.

New DLL wminet_utils, written from System.Management's open interop
declarations: the IWbemClassObject and IWbemQualifierSet methods by name
(the vtable index they pass is not needed), IWbemObjectAccess property
handles, ConnectServerWmi through the WbemLocator, the query, enumeration
and Put helpers on the IWbemServices passed in, COM security as no-ops
(SetSecurity, ResetSecurity, Bless*), GetErrorInfo, and
GetDemultiplexedStub: an IWbemObjectSink that hands each indicated object
and the status to the sink's IWmiEventSource (ManagementEventWatcher.Start()
threw InvalidCastException when handed its own object back). wine.inf puts
it in Microsoft.NET\Framework64 and Framework\v4.0.30319 (wineboot -u does
on upgrade).

Gate test-wminetutils (64- and 32-bit: the files, the 50 names, a WQL query
of Win32_OperatingSystem, the event stub); mutants SG_MUTANT_WMINET_NO_QUERY
and SG_MUTANT_WMINET_SELF_STUB fail it.
